questions.explanation:
Ultimate bearing capacity of the footing as per 
Terzaghi's equation for rectangular footing is given as [latex]
\begin{aligned}
q_{u}=&\left(1+0.3 \frac{B}{L}\right) \mathrm{cN}_{c}+\gamma \mathrm{D}_{1} \mathrm{N}_{q} \\
&+\frac{1}{2} \gamma B\left(1-0.2 \frac{\mathrm{B}}{\mathrm{L}}\right) \mathrm{N}_{y}
\end{aligned}[/latex] But for sand, c=0 [latex]
\begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad q_{u}&=(18 \times 1 \times 24)+\frac{1}{2} \times 18 \times 1.5\\
&\times\left(1-0.2 \times \frac{1.5}{3.0}\right) \times 20\\
 \Rightarrow \quad q_{u}&=432+243 \\
 \Rightarrow \quad q_{u}&=675 \mathrm{kN} / \mathrm{m}^{2} \\
\end{aligned}[/latex] The net ultimate bearing capacity. [latex]
\begin{aligned}
q_{n u} &=q_{u}-\gamma D_{t} \\
&=675-18 \times 1=657 \mathrm{kN} / \mathrm{m}^{2}
\end{aligned}[/latex]
